        "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en",
        "revisions": [
          {
            "parentid": 0,
            "revid": 8822,
            "slots": {
              "main": {
                "*": "Great! I have some ideas for census regions for Earth ([https://i.imgur.com/dOSNOVa.png here]) and Mars ([https://i.imgur.com/gc8iysL.png here]), I intend to make pages for one state in each region, to provide an idea of what each is like in various ways. One of the ways is politically, do you have any idea what the general party strength is in regions of the US? I'd figure the only strong indicaters presently would be 1) Liberationists having a strong base in the La Plata region, as it's pre-annexation population didn't flee offworld in the course of the war and 2) United Republicans might have strong presences in resettled mexican states and recently annexed states (the Borneos, South African states).",
                "contentformat": "text/x-wiki",
                "contentmodel": "wikitext"
              }
            },
            "timestamp": "2019-01-21T01:26:36Z"
          }
        ],
        "title": "Thread:YNot1989/@comment-29372813-20190110213903/@comment-29372813-20190121012636",
        "touched": "2019-01-21T01:26:36Z"
      },
      "3020": {
        "contentmodel": "wikitext",
        "lastrevid": 8824,
        "length": 602,
        "new": "",
        "ns": 1201,
        "pageid": 3020,
        "pagelanguage": "en",
        "pagelanguagedir": "ltr",
        "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en",
        "revisions": [
          {
            "parentid": 0,
            "revid": 8824,
            "slots": {
              "main": {
                "*": "Hold off on Mars' cencus regions for a while. I'm still finishing the states.\n\nThe Liberationists are only strong in northern Argentina and Mexico's central valley (which while depopoulated is still overwhelmingly Mexican. The United Republicans are strong in America's heartland, the Atlantic Seaboard down through the Deep South. The Conservative Party is popular across Mexico and the Southwest, and has a lot of Support across Canada and even New York.\n\nEastern Australia, England, and the Cape are all Conservative basions, while the rest of hose regions are held firmly by the United Republicans.",
                "contentformat": "text/x-wiki",
                "contentmodel": "wikitext"
              }
            },
            "timestamp": "2019-01-22T19:44:44Z"
          }
        ],
        "title": "Thread:YNot1989/@comment-29372813-20190110213903/@comment-899576-20190122194444",
        "touched": "2019-01-22T19:44:44Z"
      },
      "3021": {
        "contentmodel": "wikitext",
        "lastrevid": 8826,
        "length": 413,
        "ns": 1201,
        "pageid": 3021,
        "pagelanguage": "en",
        "pagelanguagedir": "ltr",
        "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en",
        "revisions": [
          {
            "parentid": 8825,
            "revid": 8826,
            "slots": {
              "main": {
                "*": "I figured as much, just my tentative thoughts about regional variation based on climate and relative isolation (maybe if some old Luongists in Araby could be firtile base for Liberationists off Earth). \n\nDo the Liberals have any significant presence in any given area? Their wiki page that they hold 111 state houses, that seems like considerable influence if it’s not just relatively disconnected happenstance.",
                "contentformat": "text/x-wiki",
                "contentmodel": "wikitext"
              }
            },
            "timestamp": "2019-01-22T21:26:04Z"
          }
        ],
